{
  "_description": "LEAST-PRIVILEGE DEPLOYMENT IDENTITY POLICY for this repository. Review artifact only: an AWS administrator must substitute the placeholders and attach it manually. This repository's tooling NEVER modifies IAM automatically. Placeholders: {{ACCOUNT_ID}} = 12-digit target account id, {{REGION}} = the target deployment region, {{STACK_NAME}} = the samconfig.toml stack_name. Scope notes: (1) CloudFormation generated physical names start with the stack name, so every template resource is scoped to '<stack name>-*' patterns; S3 bucket names are lowercased accordingly. (2) 'aws-sam-cli-managed-*' is the documented prefix of the SAM CLI's code-artifact deployment bucket (samconfig has resolve_s3 = true). (3) Both functions have no explicit Role property, so CloudFormation creates and manages the execution roles - hence the iam: role-management actions; iam:PassRole is deliberately absent because CloudFormation creates these roles inside the same stack and binds them itself. (4) One documented wildcard-resource exception: logs:PutResourcePolicy (LogsAccountLevelResourcePolicy statement) has no resource-level permission support in IAM, so it must carry Resource \"*\". Review with IAM Access Analyzer before attaching; a passing preflight (scripts/check_deployment_permissions.py) is evidence, not a guarantee - SCPs, session policies, and resource policies are outside its scope.",
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "CloudFormationStackLifecycle",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "cloudformation:CreateStack",
        "cloudformation:CreateChangeSet",
        "cloudformation:ExecuteChangeSet",
        "cloudformation:DescribeChangeSet",
        "cloudformation:DeleteChangeSet",
        "cloudformation:DescribeStacks",
        "cloudformation:DeleteStack"
      ],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:cloudformation:{{REGION}}:{{ACCOUNT_ID}}:stack/{{STACK_NAME}}/*",
        "arn:aws:cloudformation:{{REGION}}:{{ACCOUNT_ID}}:changeSet/{{STACK_NAME}}/*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "Sid": "SamManagedDeploymentBucket",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "s3:CreateBucket",
        "s3:PutObject",
        "s3:GetObject",
        "s3:ListBucket",
        "s3:GetBucketLocation",
        "s3:DeleteObject",
        "s3:DeleteBucket"
      ],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::aws-sam-cli-managed-*",
        "arn:aws:s3:::aws-sam-cli-managed-*/*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "Sid": "TemplateDocumentsBucket",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "s3:CreateBucket",
        "s3:PutEncryptionConfiguration",
        "s3:GetEncryptionConfiguration",
        "s3:PutPublicAccessBlock",
        "s3:GetPublicAccessBlock",
        "s3:DeleteBucket"
      ],
      "Resource": ["arn:aws:s3:::{{STACK_NAME}}-*"]
    },
    {
      "Sid": "TemplateDynamoDbTables",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "dynamodb:CreateTable",
        "dynamodb:DescribeTable",
        "dynamodb:DeleteTable",
        "dynamodb:TagResource"
      ],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:dynamodb:{{REGION}}:{{ACCOUNT_ID}}:table/{{STACK_NAME}}-*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "Sid": "TemplateLambdaFunctions",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "lambda:CreateFunction",
        "lambda:UpdateFunctionCode",
        "lambda:UpdateFunctionConfiguration",
        "lambda:GetFunction",
        "lambda:DeleteFunction",
        "lambda:AddPermission",
        "lambda:TagResource"
      ],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:lambda:{{REGION}}:{{ACCOUNT_ID}}:function:{{STACK_NAME}}-*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "Sid": "TemplateLambdaExecutionRoles",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "iam:CreateRole",
        "iam:GetRole",
        "iam:PutRolePolicy",
        "iam:GetRolePolicy",
        "iam:DeleteRolePolicy",
        "iam:DeleteRole",
        "iam:TagRole",
        "iam:UntagRole"
      ],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:iam::{{ACCOUNT_ID}}:role/{{STACK_NAME}}-*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "Sid": "TemplateHttpApi",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "apigatewayv2:CreateApi",
        "apigatewayv2:GetApi",
        "apigatewayv2:UpdateApi",
        "apigatewayv2:DeleteApi",
        "apigatewayv2:CreateStage",
        "apigatewayv2:GetStage",
        "apigatewayv2:UpdateStage",
        "apigatewayv2:CreateIntegration",
        "apigatewayv2:GetIntegration",
        "apigatewayv2:UpdateIntegration",
        "apigatewayv2:CreateRoute",
        "apigatewayv2:GetRoute",
        "apigatewayv2:UpdateRoute",
        "apigatewayv2:CreateAuthorizer",
        "apigatewayv2:GetAuthorizer",
        "apigatewayv2:UpdateAuthorizer",
        "apigatewayv2:DeleteAuthorizer"
      ],
      "Resource": ["arn:aws:apigateway:{{REGION}}::/apis*"]
    },
    {
      "Sid": "TemplateCognitoUserPools",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "cognito-idp:CreateUserPool",
        "cognito-idp:DescribeUserPool",
        "cognito-idp:UpdateUserPool",
        "cognito-idp:DeleteUserPool",
        "cognito-idp:TagResource",
        "cognito-idp:UntagResource",
        "cognito-idp:CreateUserPoolClient",
        "cognito-idp:DescribeUserPoolClient",
        "cognito-idp:UpdateUserPoolClient",
        "cognito-idp:DeleteUserPoolClient",
        "cognito-idp:CreateUserPoolDomain",
        "cognito-idp:DescribeUserPoolDomain",
        "cognito-idp:DeleteUserPoolDomain"
      ],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:cognito-idp:{{REGION}}:{{ACCOUNT_ID}}:userpool/{{REGION}}_*"
      ],
      "_scope_note": "Cognito user pool IDs are server-generated (region_ + random suffix), so the pool resource type cannot be scoped narrower than this region-prefix wildcard. This is a wildcard within one resource type and one account/region, NOT a global Resource '*' - user pool creation, its app client and its hosted-UI domain all live under this ARN pattern."
    },
    {
      "Sid": "TemplateAlarmsTopic",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "sns:CreateTopic",
        "sns:GetTopicAttributes",
        "sns:SetTopicAttributes",
        "sns:Subscribe",
        "sns:DeleteTopic",
        "sns:TagResource"
      ],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:sns:{{REGION}}:{{ACCOUNT_ID}}:{{STACK_NAME}}-alarms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "Sid": "TemplateCloudWatchAlarms",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "cloudwatch:PutMetricAlarm",
        "cloudwatch:DescribeAlarms",
        "cloudwatch:DeleteAlarms"
      ],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:cloudwatch:{{REGION}}:{{ACCOUNT_ID}}:alarm/{{STACK_NAME}}-*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "Sid": "TemplateLogGroups",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "logs:CreateLogGroup",
        "logs:PutRetentionPolicy",
        "logs:DeleteLogGroup"
      ],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:logs:{{REGION}}:{{ACCOUNT_ID}}:log-group:/aws/lambda/{{STACK_NAME}}-*",
        "arn:aws:logs:{{REGION}}:{{ACCOUNT_ID}}:log-group:/aws/apigateway/{{STACK_NAME}}/*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "Sid": "TemplatePagerDutySecret",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "secretsmanager:CreateSecret",
        "secretsmanager:DescribeSecret",
        "secretsmanager:UpdateSecret",
        "secretsmanager:TagResource",
        "secretsmanager:DeleteSecret"
      ],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:secretsmanager:{{REGION}}:{{ACCOUNT_ID}}:secret:{{STACK_NAME}}-pagerduty*",
        "arn:aws:secretsmanager:{{REGION}}:{{ACCOUNT_ID}}:secret:{{STACK_NAME}}-pagerduty*-*"
      ],
      "_scope_note": "Secret secret-name ARNs carry a server-generated suffix after a second dash, so both the exact-name prefix and the suffixed form are listed. Value-filling the secret (put-secret-value) is deliberately OUT of this deployment identity: it is an operator action done with a normal admin credential post-deploy, which keeps the deployment role read-only with respect to PagerDuty credentials."
    },
    {
      "Sid": "TemplateEventBridgeSchedules",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "events:PutRule",
        "events:DescribeRule",
        "events:PutTargets",
        "events:DeleteTargets",
        "events:DeleteRule",
        "events:EnableRule",
        "events:DisableRule"
      ],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:events:{{REGION}}:{{ACCOUNT_ID}}:rule/{{STACK_NAME}}*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "Sid": "LogsAccountLevelResourcePolicy",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["logs:PutResourcePolicy"],
      "Resource": ["*"],
      "_exception_note": "The ONE wildcard resource in this policy: logs:PutResourcePolicy has no resource-level permission support in IAM (a log-group ARN would grant nothing). It is required only because the template grants API Gateway write access to the API access-log group via AWS::Logs::ResourcePolicy."
    }
  ]
}